    fact: 'Children don’t react the same way to sleep deprivation as adults: while adults get sleepy, children become hyperactive. In fact, a lack of sleep can result in ADHD-like symptoms in kids. Children need an average of nine to 10 hours of sleep each night',
    category: 'Human',
    series: 'misc',
    tags: ['fact'],
    isFavorite: false,
