    fact: 'In 2015, Dr. Khurshid Guru, the director of robotic surgery at Rosewell Park Cancer Institute in New York, saved the life of a child who suffered an asthma attack aboard his transatlantic flight. Unfortunately, the parents had packed the asthma medication of their child in the checked-in luggage. Guru then made a makeshift inhaler using a plastic water bottle, a cup, some tape, an oxygen tank, and an adult inhaler to help the child breathe and saved his life.',
