    fact: "While serving as an army pharmacist for France, Antoine-Augustin Parmentier was captured by the Prussians and fed only potatoes during his captivity, known only as hog feed. He survived and emerged in good shape. He made it a personal mission to convince his countrymen of potatoes' merits. Due largely to his effort, France declared potatoes edible in 1772. His tomb in Paris is decorated with potatoes plants as a tribute.",
