    fact: "Sir Hugh Beaver, the managing director of Guinness Breweries in the 1950s, went to a shooting party. After missing the shot at a golden plover, he got into an argument. In his defense, he said that it was the fastest game bird in Europe but failed to find a reference book that could prove him right. That's when he realized that there should be a book to answer such questions. Later, he published the first Guinness World Records.",
