    fact: "Marcel Pinte, a six years old boy, was the youngest hero of the French Resistance. He acted as a courier for resistance fighters, slipping past enemy patrols and carrying messages. He died tragically in August 1944, when one of the guerrillas' Sten guns went off by accident. In 1950, he was posthumously awarded the rank of sergeant in the Resistance.",
