    fact: "In 1952, the great thick yellow smog took over London for five days and killed more than 4000 people. It was so bad that people on the street could not even see their own feet. Some of the people who died didn't suffer from any lung problems; they died by falling and drowning in the Thames as they couldn't see the river.",
