    fact: 'Medicine bottle foil seals exist because of poison. Those seals on the top of medicine bottles were put in place after a rash of poisonings occurred in 1982, in which seven people in the Chicago area were killed after ingesting Tylenol laced with potassium cyanide, which is used to kill insects.',
