    fact: "Genghis Khan used a smart policy of strategic marriages. He would marry off a daughter to the king of an allied nation. Other wives of the king were dismissed. He would then assign his new son-in-law to military duty in the Mongol wars. Most sons-in-law died in combat, and Khan's daughter would take over the rule of the kingdom.",
