    fact: "The last US Civil War widow, Helen Viola Jackson, died in 2020. In 1936, she married 93-year-old James Bolin at the age of 17. A young woman marrying an older man for his Civil War pension as a dependent was common practice in the early 20th century. Bolin died in June 1939. Jackson never remarried, didn't have any children, and also never collected her husband's pension.",
