    id: 21306,
    fact: 'In 1987, Steve Rothstein bought a golden ticket from American Airlines "” granting him a lifetime of unlimited travel. He flew more than 10 million miles and 10,000 flights. He used his power to fly hopeless strangers home, a friend to the Louvre, and a priest to Rome to meet the pope. He approached random people at the airport and offered them his companion pass (which he paid $150,000 for). He booked flights under fake names if he didn\'t know who his companion would be. In 2008, the airline accused him of fraud and terminated his lifetime pass.',
