    fact: 'An astronomer travelled to India in 1760 to observe transits of Venus. Unfavorable winds blew his ship off-course, and he missed the date. He stayed in India for eight years for the next transit of Venus, but on the day of the event, the sky became cloudy, and he saw nothing. When he returned home, he found that he had been declared legally dead and been replaced in the job. His wife had remarried, and all his relatives had plundered his estate.',
